// The compiler options a TypeScript program needs to resolve this
// codebase's own module shape — bundler resolution, isolated per-file
// transpilation, no emit, and `@/*` for this package's own root
// (`src/`) — with no opinion on `strict`, `include` or `exclude`, which
// are each consumer's own call.
//
// Published at `@moba2d/core/tsconfig.base.json` (see `package.json`'s
// `exports`) so a pack's own `tsconfig.json` can `extends` it by package
// name rather than a relative path into core's checkout, which stops
// resolving the day the pack is a repository of its own
// (content-pack-extraction batch 5 task 6 fix round 2 — `../../
// tsconfig.pack-riot.json` was exactly that relative path, the same
// defect Task 5 was found for on a different file). `tsconfig.json`
// (this package's own program) extends it too, so there is exactly one
// place these options are stated.
//
// `paths` lives here, not in each extending config, on purpose: a
// `paths` mapping declared by an `extends`-ed config is resolved
// relative to *that config file's own location*, not the extending
// config's — so `"./src/*"`, declared here, always means "core's own
// `src/`" regardless of whether the extending config is `tsconfig.json`
// two directories up or a pack's own `tsconfig.json` published as a
// separate repository. `@moba2d/core`'s exported entry points
// (`ContentApi.ts`, `content/types.ts`, ...) are core's own source,
// shipped unbundled, and internally import via `@/*` like the rest of
// this codebase — a consuming pack's typecheck has to resolve that alias
// to see real types through them (proven the hard way: without it,
// `api.MissileSpellObject`'s own methods silently degrade to errors
// two and three hops downstream of the real cause, an unresolved
// `@/managers/AssetManager` import inside `ContentApi.ts` itself).
// `packBoundary.test.ts` is the actual rule that a pack's *own* code may
// never write `@/...` — this mapping existing does not relax that; it
// only lets a pack's compiler see through core's own internals.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  }
}
